From 171e5df0182c21c7583678321aaeb6c0a8f89fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ileapp_bridge typo and replace hardcoded orchestrator
 stage list with manifest-based discovery

- Rename apps/extractors/illeap_bridge -> ileapp_bridge (matches the
  spelling used everywhere else: ileapp_record source_type, orchestrator
  stage name, schema, tests, docs). Update the package name and internal
  imports accordingly.

- apps/orchestrator/src/main.ts no longer hardcodes a STAGES array
  pointing at a packages-py/ directory that hasn't existed since the
  extractors moved to apps/extractors/ (this is why "investigate" could
  not run any stage). Stages are now discovered at startup by scanning
  apps/extractors/*/stage.json (+ the single apps/reporting/stage.json),
  validated against packages/contracts/stage-manifest.schema.json. A
  stage's name is always its directory's basename, so the orchestrator's
  stage list can no longer disagree with what's on disk. Startup fails
  fast (before any stage runs) on: an invalid manifest, a missing
  entrypoint file, two enabled stages sharing an order value, or an
  extractor stage ordered after the reporting stage.

- Add stage.json to the three existing extractors (crash, ileapp_bridge,
  mvt_iocs) and to apps/reporting. mvt_iocs is marked
  requiresResultsPath: true; runStage() now fails that stage early with a
  clear message instead of spawning a subprocess that fails on a missing
  argument.

- Document the stage.json requirement as rule 4 in EXTRACTOR_CONTRACT.md.

- Fix stale packages-py/ paths left over from the apps/ move in
  scripts/EXTRACTOR_SETUP.md and a comment in scripts/test_db_writer.py.

Not included: uv.lock still references the old verichron-illeap-bridge
package name and apps/extractors/illeap_bridge editable path. That is a
generated file -- run "uv lock" after applying this patch to regenerate
it rather than hand-editing it.
